  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 builds `Lasso(alpha, max_iter=10000, tol=1e-3, selection='random')` with `random_state` unset (global numpy stream); the v2 `lasso` predictor pins `max_iter=2000, tol=1e-2, selection='random', random_state=0`. Every setting is overridable; with the 1.6.1 values and `random_state` equal to the global seed the fitted coefficients agree to float32 precision (class forward). B5 should set max_iter=10000 and tol=1e-3 if the 1.6.1 solver is to be matched.",
    "The 1.6.1 default (first grid point) and the v2 default are both alpha=1.0, so the default is unchanged (the 1.6.1 grid is 1, 0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.1, 0.01, 5); the v2 search space is log-uniform in [1e-4, 10].",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading; the v2 `Lasso` preset consumes the whole gene expression view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`). Compared on a pre-selected matrix; the list wiring belongs to B5.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64."
  ],
